<section class="owner-confirmation">
  <div class="owner-confirmation-shell">
    <p class="owner-confirmation-eyebrow">Revenue review request received</p>
    <h1>Your 48-hour review request is in.</h1>
    <p class="owner-confirmation-lede">A real Seascape person will read what you sent. If the listing or address and what feels off are there, we can take a more useful first look right away.</p>

    <div class="owner-confirmation-panel">
      <h2>The fastest first pass needs 2 things.</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A listing link or property address.</li>
        <li>Send one sentence on what feels off: revenue, booking-site fees, reporting, owner communication, pricing, occupancy, or the current manager setup.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you skipped either one, reply to the confirmation email with it. Plain English is better than a polished explanation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="owner-confirmation-panel">
      <h2>What happens next.</h2>
      <p>We will use the evidence available, call out anything we still need, and send back a one-page revenue review with what deserves a closer look next.</p>
      <p>While you wait, the <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-fees-florida/">management-fee guide</a> and <a href="/property-management/maximize-vacation-rental-income-florida/">owner income guide</a> explain the fee and booking-source questions we usually check first.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="owner-confirmation-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/property-management/">Back to Owner Services</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/research/owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026/">Read the Owner Benchmark</a>
    </div>
    <p class="owner-confirmation-note">Need to add context now? Reply to the confirmation email with the listing link or address and a sentence or two about what feels off.</p>
  </div>
</section>
